{"text": "To achieve the target of 24 using the numbers [4, 8, 8, 11] exactly once with the operations +, -, *, /, we can use the following expression:", "start": 0, "end": 141, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(11 - 8) × 8 + 4 = 3 × 8 + 4 = 24 + 4 - 4 = 24", "start": 143, "end": 189, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So, the steps are as follows:", "start": 191, "end": 220, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1. Subtract 8 from 11: 11 - 8 = 3", "start": 221, "end": 254, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "2. Multiply the result by 8: 3 × 8 = 24", "start": 255, "end": 294, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "3. Add 4 to the result: 24 + 4 - 4 = 24", "start": 295, "end": 334, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Thus, the expression (11 - 8) × 8 + 4 gives us 24.", "start": 336, "end": 386, "label": "inform"}
